---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/cash-flow.css';
---
<Base title="Payday Planner kit: try the free preview" description="A 13-week planner for households with different paydays. Try Howloop's free cash-flow preview and explore a possible A$19 downloadable kit. Not available to buy yet.">
<div class="planner-page planner-wrap">
  <header class="planner-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="planner-kicker">HOWLOOP ORIGINAL · PRODUCT PREVIEW</p>
      <h1>A good month can still have a tight Tuesday.</h1>
      <p class="planner-lead">One payday is fortnightly. Another is monthly. The rent has its own schedule. Put them on one 13-week calendar and see the gaps between them.</p>
      <div class="planner-actions"><a class="planner-btn planner-btn--primary" href="/tools/cash-flow/" data-planner-link="planner_demo_open" data-placement="product">Try the free working preview</a></div>
      <p class="planner-small" style="margin-top:.8rem">No account. No bank connection. Your numbers stay in your browser.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="planner-picture" aria-label="Illustrative timing example">
      <h2>Same week. Different days.</h2>
      <div class="planner-timeline">
        <div class="planner-day"><span>MONDAY</span><strong>A$400</strong><small>Starting cash</small></div>
        <div class="planner-day planner-day--bill"><span>TUESDAY</span><strong>−A$250</strong><small>After A$650 rent</small></div>
        <div class="planner-day"><span>THURSDAY</span><strong>A$1,950</strong><small>After A$2,200 pay</small></div>
      </div>
      <p>Illustration only. A positive balance on Thursday does not cover Tuesday's shortfall.</p>
    </aside>
  </header>
  <section class="planner-section" aria-labelledby="preview-includes">
    <p class="planner-kicker">START WITH THE FREE PREVIEW</p><h2 id="preview-includes">See your timing, one week at a time.</h2>
    <div class="planner-steps">
      <article><span class="planner-step-number">01</span><h3>Mix your paydays</h3><p>Add weekly, fortnightly, monthly or one-off take-home income. Enter the amounts you actually expect.</p></article>
      <article><span class="planner-step-number">02</span><h3>Date the bills</h3><p>Add regular payments and known one-offs, plus the cash and buffer you choose to start with.</p></article>
      <article><span class="planner-step-number">03</span><h3>Find the low points</h3><p>Review all 13 weeks, inspect individual days, and download or print your result for free.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="planner-offer" aria-labelledby="kit-title">
    <div>
      <p class="planner-kicker">THE POSSIBLE PAID KIT</p><h2 id="kit-title">A reusable plan you can keep.</h2>
      <p>We're exploring a downloadable Payday Planner kit built around the same calculation engine. The proposed extra value is a complete repeatable workflow:</p>
      <ul><li>Side-by-side regular-pay and lower-pay scenarios</li><li>An offline working copy with plan backup and restore</li><li>A printable payday checklist and plain setup instructions</li></ul>
      <p class="planner-small" style="margin-top:1rem">These kit features are planned, not delivered by this preview. The free tools already on Howloop stay free. This page tests interest; it does not establish demand or promise a launch date.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="planner-panel">
      <span class="planner-mode">NOT AVAILABLE TO BUY</span><p class="planner-small">Price being tested</p><p class="planner-price">A$19 <span>once</span></p>
      <p class="planner-small">A proposed price for a finished download. There is no checkout, preorder or payment on this page.</p>
      <a class="planner-btn planner-btn--primary" style="margin-top:1rem" href="/tools/cash-flow/" data-planner-link="planner_demo_open" data-placement="product">Explore the free preview</a>
      <div class="planner-feedback" data-planner-feedback hidden>
        <h3>Would a finished kit be useful at A$19?</h3>
        <div class="planner-actions"><button type="button" class="planner-btn" data-feedback-choice="yes">I'd consider it</button><button type="button" class="planner-btn" data-feedback-choice="not-yet">Not yet</button></div>
        <p class="planner-small" style="margin-top:.6rem">Optional feedback is recorded only if you've allowed analytics. We don't ask for an email or your financial numbers.</p>
        <p class="planner-small" data-feedback-status role="status"></p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <section class="planner-section" aria-labelledby="planner-questions"><h2 id="planner-questions">Before you start.</h2>
    <details class="planner-faq"><summary>Who is this for?</summary><p>Households that know their expected take-home pay and bills but want to see when money arrives and leaves. It may be especially useful when two people are paid on different schedules. It only models the entries you include.</p></details>
    <details class="planner-faq"><summary>Does this tell me what I can afford?</summary><p>No. This is a calendar and arithmetic tool, not a recommendation, lending decision or guarantee. It does not calculate tax, interest, overdraft fees, benefits or changes in prices. Check actual dates and amounts with your providers.</p></details>
    <details class="planner-faq"><summary>What happens when pay and bills fall on the same day?</summary><p>The preview shows end-of-day balances and a separate conservative low that treats that day's bills as leaving before pay arrives. It cannot know the order your bank will process transactions. It does not shift dates for weekends or public holidays.</p></details>
    <details class="planner-faq"><summary>Are my numbers uploaded?</summary><p>No. The planner calculates in your browser. Saving is optional and local to that browser. Downloads and printed copies may contain your entries, so keep them private. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy details</a>.</p></details>
  </section>
</div>
<script>import '../../scripts/product-events.mjs';</script>
</Base>
